[
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "My stomach would still be in knots, because I'm someone who never touches equipment",
    "sys_rule_justification": "if you can save lives at no risk to anyone, you have to.",
    "pda_responsibility": "if I freeze, whatever happens to those five workers is partly my doing.",
    "pda_repair_intention": "then I tell staff exactly what I did."
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "part of me would feel sick about overriding railway controls",
    "sys_rule_justification": "a duty to prevent serious harm when it costs nobody anything outranks a sign",
    "pda_responsibility": "The moment I notice that lever, I'm in control of how this ends."
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "I'd do it, though I'd be shaking.",
    "sys_rule_justification": "people's lives come before protocol when the rescue harms no one.",
    "pda_responsibility": "staying still would be my decision too.",
    "pda_repair_intention": "then flag down whoever's in charge and own it."
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "my first reaction would be panic about meddling with something I have no business touching.",
    "sys_rule_justification": "If you can stop a disaster without hurting anybody, you're obliged to.",
    "pda_responsibility": "I can reach it, I know what it does, so the outcome is in my hands.",
    "pda_repair_intention": "then go find help and explain."
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "I'd feel pulled two ways, because I was raised never to tamper with public equipment",
    "sys_rule_justification": "rescuing people who are about to be hit, when it endangers no one, is a basic obligation",
    "pda_responsibility": "Knowing what the lever does makes me responsible for using it.",
    "pda_repair_intention": "then I report it right away."
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "my hands wouldn't stop trembling. It feels wrong to seize control of trains",
    "sys_rule_justification": "the right of those five workers not to be run down",
    "pda_responsibility": "If I do nothing, that's still me deciding their fate"
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "The tension for me is real, since I'd be breaking a rule I normally defend",
    "sys_rule_justification": "preventing avoidable harm is a duty, not an option.",
    "pda_responsibility": "being right there, with the power to change it, puts the result squarely on me."
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "doing something drastic with unfamiliar equipment clashes with everything in me",
    "sys_rule_justification": "There's a clear duty to help when helping is safe.",
    "pda_responsibility": "Whatever happens next follows from what I do at that lever"
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "Inside, though, I'd be scrambling, because I believe strongly in not overstepping",
    "sys_rule_justification": "you must never let people die when saving them costs no one anything.",
    "pda_responsibility": "inaction would be my choice as much as action."
  },
  {
    "pd_decision_conflict": "torn between respecting rules about restricted equipment and the obvious need to stop that train.",
    "sys_rule_justification": "when a life can be protected at no cost to anyone, you're bound to protect it.",
    "pda_responsibility": "Being the one beside the lever means the outcome runs through me",
    "pda_repair_intention": "make sure someone official hears the whole story."
  }
]
